A||||5||mrfixit58||A Two Fiero Family?||||10||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||08-11-2001||10:35 PM||||Well you could have knocked me over with a feather...<P>While driving to a restaurant in the Buick with the two kids in the back, the topic of Fieros came up. Not that this is unusual or anything. During a moment of levity I joking-ly told my wife that the old tired GT in the back yard was for her. She laughed and said, "yea, right!". About that time we pulled into the parking lot.<P>We met up with th family and was having a nice dinner. My brother, who is about to head out to southern California for work, mentioned he would be looking for a classic car to bring home but, unlike me, he wants to buy one that already restored so he won't have to work on it.<P>Before I could even comment, my wife perks up and says, "Roy want to build me a Fiero now". Every one but me just kind of nodded politely and the conversation went another direction.<P>When we got back into the Buick and started heading for home, I asked her if she was serious about wanting a Fiero of her own and she said "Sure!". Like I said... knock me over with a feather!"<P>So, it looks like there's going to be a black GT with tan interior in our future! I'm so giddy I feel like I should be passing out cigars!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Wish me luck,<P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||California Kid||08-11-2001||10:54 PM||||Hey Roy, Good luck on your Fiero search!!<P>Just a suggestion, but you may want to stay away from Black, it's impossible to keep clean and the plastic panels act like dust magnets (reason I changed mine from Black to Viper Yellow).  Also, the darker the paint the more any of the waves in the panels will be more visible.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||08-12-2001||08:19 AM||||Hey Fixit!<BR>Good job!<BR>I finally have my wife driving a Fiero and she is loving it!<BR>Some times we have to meet up some where, and it is a blast to have two gold Fieros parked side by side!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||08-12-2001||12:22 PM||||California - Yea, black isn't my color of choice either. She mentioned either red or black. The car I have is already black so I thought it'd be easier to just do a re-paint rather that a color change. We'll see when the time comes.<P>'wrecker - This wouldn't be her first Fiero. We had an 85 GT we bought in 86 and put 80,000 miles on it before I got stupid and bought an 85 Corvette (that's another story for another day in another thread). The neat part is I've never actually built a car for HER. But... she's never asked me to. It should be fun.<P>I'll post when the project starts.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||6
